From bc764301c0f74cae379a0a6d19b8d04dcb893f8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:58:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] workspace_source v2: own external worktrees, bound
 premanifest recovery, gate initial on enabled

Review t_6ed792ebc90606ce on PR #3307:

- P1: initial registration checks other live tasks' source-journal paths
  (not only tasks.workspace_path) and rechecks inside the observation write
  transaction, so two scratch tasks cannot register one external worktree.
  A definitely refused observation and done/archived tasks own nothing.
- P2: premanifest predecessor recovery takes the resolver's materialize
  budget through local git reads and the origin proof; artifact verification
  reuses the recovered predecessor instead of re-proving it; the resolver
  checks the budget before a successful return (zero-artifact included).
- P3: register_initial refuses source_disabled before persistence or RPC
  when kanban.workspace_source is disabled (heartbeat surface covered).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_source_ownership_budget.py (9; RED 7 on
the previous head, the 2 controls pass on both).
